  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Resilience of Conflict-Affected Communities in Kachin and Northern Shan States Through Increased Safe and Rewarding Migration (SAFE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support internally displaced persons and members of host communities in Kachin and Northern Shan states to enjoy safer labour mobility and reduced vulnerability to human trafficking and associated forms of exploitation and abuse. During the COVID-19 pandemic, the SAFE project has received additional funding to implement COVID-19 prevention and response in SAFE target areas. Through the additional funding the project aims to target the immediate needs of the returning migrants before and during their quarantine period of 21 days in government or community-based facilities in SAFE target areas. The immediate support includes food, hygiene items and other non-food items such as bedding kits. The project also aims to conduct risk communication and community engagement through COVID-19 awareness sessions and aim to collect information on the situation for returning migrants through the roll out of a rapid assessment in Kachin State.</narrative>
  </description>
